  "reason": "The current best configuration (config_021: multimodal, multiprofile, scvi_n200, imagenet_vit_l, transformer, weighted; acc=0.725) has only been tested with 'weighted' fusion. The fusion strategy is a critical design decision that determines how RNA and image representations are combined, yet no high-performing configuration has used 'concat' fusion. Config_031 is an exact single-variable comparison to config_021, changing only fusion from weighted to concat while holding all other settings (scvi_n200, imagenet_vit_l, transformer aggregation, multiprofile) constant. This cleanly isolates the effect of fusion strategy. If concat outperforms weighted, it reveals that a learned combination is superior and opens a new optimization direction; if it underperforms, it confirms weighted fusion is the right choice and redirects budget toward other untested dimensions (e.g., image encoder or RNA encoder). Under a limited budget, resolving this fundamental architectural question with a controlled A/B comparison is more informative than exploring a second variable simultaneously."
